  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & ={e}^{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we let ${e}^{c}={r}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surfaces form a family of spheres centered at the origin.",
